WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.210
Contoso Hospitality. Disruption recovery, with Cowork and Dynamics 365.

2
00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.528
Six forty p.m. A storm closes the airport. Duty manager Amara Okafor opens Cowork.

3
00:00:10.528 --> 00:00:11.914
Her briefing is ready:

4
00:00:11.914 --> 00:00:16.200
two hundred twelve arrivals at risk, and forty-eight rooms oversold.

5
00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:18.142
She asks for a recovery plan.

6
00:00:18.142 --> 00:00:24.940
Cowork reads the guest records and loyalty tiers in Dynamics 365, and returns a plan she approves in one step.

7
00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:29.651
The guest agent, running in Dynamics 365 Contact Center, reaches every guest.

8
00:00:29.651 --> 00:00:35.160
Daniel, stuck at the gate, taps once to extend his stay, and the booking updates in Dynamics.

9
00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:36.608
Nine guests need a person.

10
00:00:36.608 --> 00:00:40.600
Customer Service routes each case to Mei at the front desk, with the full story.

11
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:46.060
Revenue manager Priya Shah sees the stranded demand in Cowork, and moves tomorrow's rates tonight.

12
00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:52.630
By seven a.m., CEO Elena Marquez has the recovery cost, guest sentiment, and an updated playbook.

13
00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:57.824
Dynamics runs the transaction. Agents do the work. Cowork is where people decide.

14
00:00:57.824 --> 00:00:59.132
Hours become minutes.

